---@field maximumPageSize? aws.swf.PageSize The maximum number of results that are returned per call. Use nextPageToken to obtain further pages of results.
---@field reverseOrder? aws.swf.ReverseOrder When set to true, returns the results in reverse order. By default, the results are returned in ascending alphabetical order by name of the activity types.

---@class aws.swf.ListClosedWorkflowExecutionsInput
---@field domain aws.swf.DomainName The name of the domain that contains the workflow executions to list.
---@field startTimeFilter? aws.swf.ExecutionTimeFilter If specified, the workflow executions are included in the returned results based on whether their start times are within the range specified by this filter. Also, if this parameter is specified, the returned results are ordered by their start times.
---@field closeTimeFilter? aws.swf.ExecutionTimeFilter If specified, the workflow executions are included in the returned results based on whether their close times are within the range specified by this filter. Also, if this parameter is specified, the returned results are ordered by their close times.
---@field executionFilter? aws.swf.WorkflowExecutionFilter If specified, only workflow executions matching the workflow ID specified in the filter are returned.
---@field closeStatusFilter? aws.swf.CloseStatusFilter If specified, only workflow executions that match this close status are listed. For example, if TERMINATED is specified, then only TERMINATED workflow executions are listed.
---@field typeFilter? aws.swf.WorkflowTypeFilter If specified, only executions of the type specified in the filter are returned.
---@field tagFilter? aws.swf.TagFilter If specified, only executions that have the matching tag are listed.
---@field nextPageToken? aws.swf.PageToken If NextPageToken is returned there are more results available. The value of NextPageToken is a unique pagination token for each page. Make the call again using the returned token to retrieve the next page. Keep all other arguments unchanged. Each pagination token expires after 24 hours. Using an expired pagination token will return a 400 error: "Specified token has exceeded its maximum lifetime".
---@field maximumPageSize? aws.swf.PageSize The maximum number of results that are returned per call. Use nextPageToken to obtain further pages of results.
---@field reverseOrder? aws.swf.ReverseOrder When set to true, returns the results in reverse order. By default the results are returned in descending order of the start or the close time of the executions.

